{
  "dom_id": "step-q117880",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Find an expression for the volume $V$ of a cylinder in terms of its height $h,$ given that the ratio of the radius of the base to the height of the cylinder is $8.$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the fact that the ratio of the radius $r$ of the base to the height $h$ is $8,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{r}{h}=8.\n$$\n\nOur goal is to express $V$ in terms of $h.$ Therefore, we need to isolate $r$ in the above equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{h} & =8 \\\\ r & =8h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe volume of a cylinder with radius $r$ and height $h$ is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nTherefore, substituting $r=8h$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {r}^{2}h \\\\  & =\\pi (8h)^{2}\\cdot h \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot 64{h}^{2}\\cdot h \\\\  & =64\\pi {h}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
